{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00397",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.02,
      "end_seconds": 6.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Ready for you, doctor. I'll stay in case you need anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.68,
      "end_seconds": 11.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 12.5,
      "end_seconds": 18.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.18,
      "end_seconds": 24.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 25.18,
      "end_seconds": 28.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Doctor, it's swelling. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.97,
      "end_seconds": 36.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.34,
      "end_seconds": 64.63,
      "duration_seconds": 26.29,
      "text": "Pretty mild, if I'm being honest. Elevation helps a bit. As for difficulty walking, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. As for difficulty walking, mostly mild. Oh, and a twist during football. That's been about the same, three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.75,
      "end_seconds": 71.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "Right, have you had swelling before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.31,
      "end_seconds": 78.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "A bit, last winter. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 80.32,
      "end_seconds": 82.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Yes, exactly like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.53,
      "end_seconds": 89.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.7,
      "end_seconds": 98.64,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "I take levetiracetam, 500 milligrams, twice a day. It's Thyronorm, 50 micrograms, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.26,
      "end_seconds": 101.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Is that long-standing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.49,
      "end_seconds": 109.8,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "About a month now. Omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day for the reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 111.53,
      "end_seconds": 117.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "That's what's prescribed, but I'm not sure she takes it every day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.02,
      "end_seconds": 123.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "I'm on Volini spray, a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.63,
      "end_seconds": 125.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Right. Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.58,
      "end_seconds": 129.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "I don't drink at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.95,
      "end_seconds": 132.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "How do you eat, generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.49,
      "end_seconds": 136.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "I skip breakfast most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.7,
      "end_seconds": 139.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.79,
      "end_seconds": 145.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Uh, just my appendix out, about eight years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.49,
      "end_seconds": 150.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.92,
      "end_seconds": 160.88,
      "duration_seconds": 8.96,
      "text": "I have epilepsy, for nearly five years. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.33,
      "end_seconds": 165.03,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.47,
      "end_seconds": 171.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "I've had an underactive thyroid, yes. I've got acid reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.38,
      "end_seconds": 173.08,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Yes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.78,
      "end_seconds": 184.29,
      "duration_seconds": 9.51,
      "text": "Alright, acid reflux, that matches what I have here. Have you ever reacted badly to a medicine or food? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.47,
      "end_seconds": 193.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "Yes, penicillin. I get hives. Yes, shellfish. I get hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.21,
      "end_seconds": 216.59,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "Any fever, pop or crack, pain in the knee or pain at the back of the heel?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.11,
      "end_seconds": 231.93,
      "duration_seconds": 14.82,
      "text": "No, no fever, no pop or crack, no pain in the knee. I did have pain in my right ankle at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.93,
      "end_seconds": 235.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.41,
      "end_seconds": 238.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 239.33,
      "end_seconds": 253.86,
      "duration_seconds": 14.53,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Blood pressure 120 over 79, weight 59 kilos. Heart rate 72, temp 36.9 degrees, BMI works out to 25.2, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, height 153 centimetres, respiratory rate 16."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.1,
      "end_seconds": 255.8,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.26,
      "end_seconds": 261.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Let me examine, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.87,
      "end_seconds": 272.78,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.78,
      "end_seconds": 275.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Tell me if anything hurts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.05,
      "end_seconds": 292.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "There's swelling and bruising on the outer side of the ankle, tender over the ligament."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.88,
      "end_seconds": 296.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Just relax, I'll be quick."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.56,
      "end_seconds": 316.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.44,
      "text": "The bones themselves aren't tender and the ankle feels stable when I test it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.02,
      "end_seconds": 336.13,
      "duration_seconds": 18.11,
      "text": "Right, thanks, please take a seat again. Let me tell you where I've got to. This is probably an ankle sprain. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I'd also keep a ligament tear in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 337.94,
      "end_seconds": 340.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Doctor, is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.28,
      "end_seconds": 358.83,
      "duration_seconds": 17.55,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's an ankle sprain, and we'll know more once the an X-ray of the ankle is back. I'd like to arrange an X-ray of the ankle for ankle injury."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_6",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 360.17,
      "end_seconds": 364.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "I can book that for Thursday at 11:30 am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.03,
      "end_seconds": 368.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Okay, so okay, I'll be there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.94,
      "end_seconds": 394.28,
      "duration_seconds": 25.34,
      "text": "I'll start you on paracetamol, 650 milligrams, three times a day, for three days. It's for ankle pain. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Rest, ice for twenty minutes at a time, a compression bandage and keep the foot up. Let's get you seen by physiotherapy, I'll arrange the letter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.02,
      "end_seconds": 398.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.72,
      "end_seconds": 408.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "I'll want another look in two weeks. Take care, and call us if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 409.92,
      "end_seconds": 412.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Nothing more from me, thanks."
    }
  ]
}